# Contact form.
#
# The form posts to /api/kontakt. Without the two required variables the route
# answers 503, and the form tells the visitor it cannot send and hands them the
# finished message to copy or open in their own mail app — no enquiry is lost,
# but none of them reach an inbox automatically either. Set these in the Vercel
# project settings before the site takes traffic.

# Required. An API key from resend.com.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Required. A verified sender on a domain you own, e.g. "Kestro <noreply@kestro.dk>".
CONTACT_FROM=
# Optional. Where enquiries land. Defaults to company.email in lib/company.ts.
CONTACT_TO=

# Optional. Every enquiry is also posted as JSON here — a CRM inbound hook
# (HubSpot, Pipedrive), an automation (Make, Zapier), or a sheet. Failures are
# logged and ignored; the email is the source of truth.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Optional. Sent as "Authorization: Bearer …" with the webhook.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# Search engine ownership.
#
# Not secrets — a verification token is a public claim of ownership and is
# visible in the page source of every verified site. They are variables
# because they differ per property, so verifying is a setting and a redeploy
# rather than a commit.
#
# Without a verified property there is no record of a single search
# impression, click, position or crawl error anywhere: Google keeps that data
# and only shows it to the verified owner. DNS verification is the better
# route where the domain's records are reachable — this is the fallback that
# works from the site itself.

# Optional. The content of the google-site-verification tag from Search Console.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=
# Optional. The content of the msvalidate.01 tag from Bing Webmaster Tools.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=
